\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (b)\u8195?\~Nuclear fusion of deuterium is difficult to achieve on Earth because of the high temperature needed.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi0 Electricity is used to increase the temperature of 4.0 g of deuterium by 50 000 000 \'b0C.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567 specific heat capacity of deuterium = 5200 J/kg \'b0C\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567 Calculate the energy needed to increase the temperature of the deuterium by 50 000 000 \'b0C.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567 Use the Physics Equations Sheet.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (3)\par
