\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb0\sa0\li567\ri567 Radioactive waste from nuclear power stations is a man-made source of background radiation.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (a)\u8195?\~Give \b one\b0  other man-made source of background radiation.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0 (1)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li567\ri567 Nuclear power stations use the energy released by nuclear fission to generate electricity.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (b)\u8195?\~Give the name of \b one\b0  nuclear fuel.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0 (1)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (c)\u8195?\~Nuclear fission releases energy.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi0 Describe the process of nuclear fission inside a nuclear reactor.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (4)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (d)\u8195?\~A new type of power station is being developed that will generate electricity using nuclear fusion.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi0 Explain how the process of nuclear fusion leads to the release of energy.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (2)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (e)\u8195?\~Nuclear fusion power stations will produce radioactive waste. This waste will have a much shorter half-life than the radioactive waste from a nuclear fission power station.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi0 Explain the advantage of the radioactive waste having a shorter half-life.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (2)\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0 (Total 10 marks)\par
