\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567 During the process of nuclear fission, a uranium ___________________\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567 absorbs a ___________________ .\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567 Electromagnetic radiation is released in the form of ___________________ .\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (3)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (b)\u8195?\~The UK needs at least 25 000 000 kW of electrical power at any time.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi0 A nuclear power station has an electrical power output of 2 400 000 kW\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567 Calculate how many nuclear power stations are needed to provide 25 000 000 kW of electrical power.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (2)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (c)\u8195?\~State \b two\b0  environmental issues caused by generating electricity using nuclear power stations.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0 (2)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (d)\u8195?\~The UK currently generates a lot of electricity by burning natural gas. This process releases carbon dioxide into the atmosphere.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi0 Figure 2\b0  shows how the concentration of carbon dioxide in the atmosphere has changed over the past 115 years.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b\ltrpar\qc\sb240\sa0\li0\ri0 Figure 2\par
\qc\sb240\sa0{\pict\jpegblip\picw7860\pich4125\picwgoal7860\pichgoal4125\picscalex100\picscaley100
}\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567 Figure 3\b0  shows how the global temperature has changed over the past 115 years.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b\ltrpar\qc\sb240\sa0\li0\ri0 Figure 3\par
\qc\sb240\sa0{\pict\jpegblip\picw7455\pich4095\picwgoal7455\pichgoal4095\picscalex100\picscaley100
}\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567 Give \b one\b0  similarity and \b one\b0  difference between the data in \b Figure 2\b0  and \b Figure 3\b0 .\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (2)\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0 (Total 9 marks)\par
\f1\fs27\cf1\ltrpar\ql\sb450\sa45\li150\ri45 Q9.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb0\sa0\li567\ri567 Nuclear power stations generate electricity through nuclear fission. Electricity can also be generated by burning shale gas.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (a)\u8195?\~Shale gas is natural gas trapped in rocks. Shale gas can be extracted by a process called fracking. There is some evidence that fracking causes minor earthquakes. Burning shale gas adds carbon dioxide to the atmosphere.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi0 Describe the advantages of nuclear power compared with the use of shale gas to generate electricity.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (3)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (b)\u8195?\~What is the name of \b one\b0  fuel used in nuclear power stations?\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0 (1)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (c)\u8195?\~Describe the process of nuclear fission.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0 (4)\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0 (Total 8 marks)\par
\f1\fs27\cf1\ltrpar\ql\sb450\sa45\li150\ri45 Q10.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb0\sa0\li567\ri567 Nuclear fission and nuclear fusion are two processes that release energy.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (a)\~\~\~\~ The following nuclear equation represents the fission of uranium-235 (U-235).\par
\qc\sb240\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0{\pict\jpegblip\picw7080\pich585\picwgoal7080\pichgoal585\picscalex100\picscaley100
}\~\par
