\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 \u8226?\~\~\~\~\~\~\~ Ba = barium\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 \u8226?\~\~\~\~\~\~\~ Kr = krypton\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 \u8226?\~\~\~\~\~\~\~ {\pict\jpegblip\picw240\pich375\picwgoal240\pichgoal375\picscalex100\picscaley100
}\~= neutron\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi0 Describe the process of nuclear fission.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567 Use the information in the equation.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (4)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (b)\~\~\~\~ Explain what happens in the process of nuclear fusion.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0 (3)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (c)\~\~\~\~ Fission reactors are used in nuclear power stations.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi0 Engineers are developing fusion reactors for use in power stations.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567 Fusion uses isotopes of hydrogen called deuterium and tritium.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 \u8226?\~\~\~\~\~\~\~ Deuterium is naturally occurring and can be easily extracted from seawater.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 \u8226?\~\~\~\~\~\~\~ Tritium can be produced from lithium. Lithium is also found in seawater.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi0 The table shows the energy released from 1 kg of fusion fuel and from 1 kg of fission fuel.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb0\sa0\li0\ri0 \~\par

