\f1\fs27\cf1\ltrpar\ql\sb450\sa45\li150\ri45 Q12.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb0\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (a)\~\~\~\~ Brown dwarf stars are thought to have been formed in the same way as other stars.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb0\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi0 They are too small for nuclear fusion reactions to take place in them.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb0\sa0\li1134\ri567 Brown dwarf stars emit infrared radiation but are not hot enough to emit visible light.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (i)\~\~\~\~\~ Describe how a star is formed.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0 (2)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (ii)\~\~\~\~ Describe the process of nuclear fusion.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0 (1)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (iii)\~\~\~\~ Scientists predicted that brown dwarf stars existed before the first one was discovered in 1995.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi0 Suggest \b one\b0  reason why scientists are now able to observe and identify brown dwarf stars.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (1)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (b)\~\~\~\~ In the 18th century some scientists suggested a theory about how the planets formed in the Solar System. The theory was that after the Sun formed, there were cool discs of matter rotating around the Sun. These cool discs of matter formed the planets. The scientists thought this must have happened around other stars too.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (i)\~\~\~\~\~ Thinking about this theory, what would the scientists have predicted to have been formed in other parts of the Universe?\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0 (1)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (ii)\~\~\~\~ Since the 1980s scientists studying young stars have shown the stars to be surrounded by cool discs of rotating matter.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi0 What was the importance of these observations to the theory the scientists suggested in the 18th century?\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (1)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (c)\~\~\~\~ The Earth contains elements heavier than iron.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi0 Why is the presence of elements heavier than iron in the Earth evidence that the Solar System was formed from material produced after a massive star exploded?\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (1)\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0 (Total 7 marks)\par
\f1\fs27\cf1\ltrpar\ql\sb450\sa45\li150\ri45 Q13.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb0\sa0\li567\ri567 Atoms are different sizes.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li567\ri567 One of the heaviest naturally occurring stable elements is lead.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li567\ri567 Two of its isotopes are lead-206 ({\pict\pngblip\picw840\pich660\picwgoal840\pichgoal660\picscalex100\picscaley100
}) and lead-208 ({\pict\pngblip\picw810\pich645\picwgoal810\pichgoal645\picscalex100\picscaley100
}).\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-1134 (a)\~\~\~\~\~(i)\~\~\~\~\~\~What is meant by \u8216?isotopes\u8217??\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0 (2)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (ii)\~\~\~\~\~How many protons are in the nucleus of a {\pict\pngblip\picw840\pich660\picwgoal840\pichgoal660\picscalex100\picscaley100
} atom?\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0 (1)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (iii)\~\~\~\~How many neutrons are in the nucleus of a {\pict\pngblip\picw840\pich660\picwgoal840\pichgoal660\picscalex100\picscaley100
} atom?\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0 (1)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (b)\~\~\~\~\~A nucleus can be accelerated in a particle accelerator and directed at a large nucleus. This produces a heavy nucleus that will decay after a short time.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi0 This is shown in \b Figure 1\b0 .\par
\qc\sb240\sa0\li0\ri0{\pict\pngblip\picw5865\pich2250\picwgoal5865\pichgoal2250\picscalex100\picscaley100
}\~\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (i)\~\~\~\~\~\~In 1984, nuclei of iron (Fe) were directed at nuclei of lead (Pb). This produced nuclei of hassium (Hs).\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi0 Complete the equation for this reaction by writing numbers in the empty boxes.\par
\qc\sb240\sa0\li0\ri0{\pict\pngblip\picw5145\pich930\picwgoal5145\pichgoal930\picscalex100\picscaley100
}\~\par
