\f1\fs27\cf1\ltrpar\ql\sb450\sa45\li150\ri45 Q15.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb0\sa0\li567\ri567 Many countries use nuclear power stations to generate electricity.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb0\sa0\li567\ri567 Nuclear power stations use the process of nuclear fission to release energy.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-1134 (a)\~\~\~\~ (i)\~\~\~\~\~\~What is nuclear fission?\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0 (1)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (ii)\~\~\~\~\~Plutonium-239 is one substance used as a fuel in a nuclear reactor. For nuclear fission to happen, the nucleus must absorb a particle.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi0 What type of particle must be absorbed?\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (1)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (b) \~\~\~\~Nuclear \b fusion\b0  also releases energy.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb0\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi0 Nuclear fusion happens at very high temperatures. A high temperature is needed to overcome the repulsion force between the nuclei.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567 (i)\~\~\~\~\~\~Why is there a repulsion force between the nuclei of atoms?\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (1)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (ii)\~\~\~\~\~Where does nuclear fusion happen naturally?\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0 (1)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (c) \~\~\~\~In 1991, scientists produced the first controlled release of energy from an experimental nuclear \b fusion\b0  reactor. This was achieved by fusing the hydrogen isotopes, deuterium and tritium.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi0 Deuterium is naturally occurring and can easily be extracted from seawater. Tritium can be produced from lithium. Lithium is also found in seawater.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567 The table gives the energy released from 1 kg of fusion fuel and from 1 kg of fission fuel.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb0\sa0\li0\ri0 \~\par

