\f1\fs22\cf0\nosupersub\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (i)\~\~\~\~\~\~Suggest \b two\b0  advantages of the fuel used in a fusion reactor compared with plutonium and the other substances used as fuel in a fission reactor.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0 (2)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (ii)\~\~\~\~\~Some scientists think that by the year 2050 a nuclear fusion power station capable of generating electricity on a large scale will have been developed.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi0 Suggest \b one\b0  important consequence of developing nuclear fusion power stations to generate electricity.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (1)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (d) \~\~\~\~Tritium is radioactive.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi0 After 36 years, only 10 g of tritium remains from an original sample of 80 g.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567 Calculate the half-life of tritium.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567 Show clearly how you work out your answer.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (2)\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0 (Total 9 marks)\par
