\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567 Which \b one\b0  of the stars, \b J\b0 , \b K\b0  or \b L\b0 , will become a black dwarf?\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567 Give a reason for your answer.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (2)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (b) \~\~\~\~Scientists can take the measurements needed to calculate the mass of many stars.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi0 Scientists cannot calculate the mass of the star Betelgeuse.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567 They estimate that the star has a mass between 8 and 20 times the mass of the Sun.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (i)\~\~\~\~\~\~Betelgeuse is in the red super giant stage of its life cycle.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi0 What will happen to Betelgeuse at the end of the red super giant stage?\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (1)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (ii)\~\~\~\~Suggest \b one\b0  reason why scientists can only estimate and \b not\b0  calculate the mass of Betelgeuse.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0 (1)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (iii)\~\~\~\~In the future, it may become possible for scientists to calculate the mass of Betelgeuse.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi0 Suggest \b one\b0  reason why.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (1)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (c) \~\~\~\~Describe what happens to a star, after the main sequence period, for the star to eventually become a \b black dwarf\b0 .\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0 (5)\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0 (Total 10 marks)\par
\f1\fs27\cf1\ltrpar\ql\sb450\sa45\li150\ri45 Q17.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb0\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (a)\~\~\~\~ There are many isotopes of the element molybdenum (Mo).\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi0 What do the nuclei of different molybdenum isotopes have in common?\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (1)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (b) \~\~\~\~The isotope molybdenum-99 is produced inside some nuclear power stations from the nuclear fission of uranium-235.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (i)\~\~\~\~\~\~What happens during the process of nuclear fission?\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0 (1)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (ii)\~\~\~\~\~Inside which part of a nuclear power station would molybdenum be produced?\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0 (1)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (c) \~\~\~\~When the nucleus of a molybdenum-99 atom decays, it emits radiation and changes into a nucleus of technetium-99.\par
\qc\sb240\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0{\pict\pngblip\picw255\pich555\picwgoal255\pichgoal555\picscalex100\picscaley100
}\fs36 Mo\fs22 \~\~\~\~{\pict\pngblip\picw690\pich120\picwgoal690\pichgoal120\picscalex100\picscaley100
}\~\~\~\~{\pict\pngblip\picw240\pich570\picwgoal240\pichgoal570\picscalex100\picscaley100
}\fs36 Tc\fs22 \~\~\~\~+\~\~\~\~Radiation\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567 What type of radiation is emitted by molybdenum-99?\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567 Give a reason for your answer.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (2)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (d) \~\~\~\~Technetium-99 has a short half-life and emits gamma radiation.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi0 What is meant by the term \u8216?half-life\u8217??\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (1)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (e) \~\~\~\~Technetium-99 is used by doctors as a medical tracer. In hospitals it is produced inside a technetium generator by the decay of molybdenum-99 nuclei.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (i)\~\~\~\~\~\~The figure below shows how the number of nuclei in a sample of molybdenum-99 changes with time as the nuclei decay.\par
\qc\sb240\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0{\pict\pngblip\picw8235\pich5955\picwgoal8235\pichgoal5955\picscalex100\picscaley100
}\line
\~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~Time in days\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567 A technetium generator will continue to produce sufficient technetium-99 until 80% of the original molybdenum nuclei have decayed.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567 After how many days will a source of molybdenum-99 inside a technetium-99 generator need replacing?\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567 Show clearly your calculation and how you use the graph to obtain your answer.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (2)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (ii)\~\~\~\~\~Medical tracers are injected into a patient\u8217?s body; this involves some risk to the patient\u8217?s health.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi0 Explain the risk to the patient of using a radioactive substance as a medical tracer.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (2)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (iii)\~\~\~\~Even though there may be a risk, doctors frequently use radioactive substances for medical diagnosis and treatments.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi0 Suggest why.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (1)\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0 (Total 11 marks)\par
\f1\fs27\cf1\ltrpar\ql\sb450\sa45\li150\ri45 Q18.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb0\sa0\li567\ri567 Nuclear fission and nuclear fusion are two processes that release energy.\par
