\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567 Nuclear fission takes place within a ____________________________ .\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567 Nuclear fusion takes place within a _____________________________ .\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (2)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (ii)\~\~\~\~\~State \b one\b0  way in which the process of nuclear fusion differs from the process of nuclear fission.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0 (1)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (b)\~\~\~\~ The following nuclear equation represents the fission of uranium-235 (U-235).\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi0 \~{\pict\pngblip\picw7065\pich375\picwgoal7065\pichgoal375\picscalex100\picscaley100
}\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567 Chemical symbols:\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567 \~\~\~\~\~\~\~ \~\~\~\~\~\~\~ Ba - barium\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567 \~\~\~\~\~\~\~ \~\~\~\~\~\~\~ Kr - krypton\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (i)\~\~\~\~\~\~Use the information in the equation to describe the process of nuclear fission.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0 (4)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (ii)\~\~\~\~\~An isotope of barium is Ba-139.\line
Ba-139 decays by beta decay to lanthanum-139 (La-139).\par
