\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb0\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (a)\~\~\~\~ Nuclear fuels and the wind are two of the energy sources used to generate electricity in the UK.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi0 Explain the advantages of using energy from nuclear fuels to generate electricity rather than using energy from the wind.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567 Include in your answer a brief description of the process used to generate electricity from nuclear fuels.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (4)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (b) \~\~\~\~In the UK, most electricity is generated in power stations that emit carbon dioxide into the atmosphere. The impact of these power stations on the environment could be reduced by the increased use of 'carbon capture' technology.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi0 Describe how 'carbon capture' would prevent the build-up of carbon dioxide in the atmosphere.\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0 (2)\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0 (Total 6 marks)\par
