\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1134\ri567\fi-567 (c)\~\~\~\~ Uranium has two natural isotopes, uranium-235 and uranium-238.\line
Uranium-235 is used as a fuel inside a nuclear reactor.\line
Inside the reactor, atoms of uranium-235 are split and energy is released.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (i)\~\~\~\~\~ How is the structure of an atom of uranium-235 different from the structure of an atom of uranium-238?\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0 (1)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (ii)\~\~\~\~ The nucleus of a uranium-235 atom must absorb a particle before the atom is able to split.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 \~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~ What type of particle is absorbed?\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0 (1)\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\b0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 (iii)\~\~\~\~ The nucleus of an atom splits into smaller parts in a reactor.\par
\f1\fs22\cf0\ltrpar\ql\sb240\sa0\li1701\ri567\fi-567 \~\~\~\~\~\~\~\~ What name is given to this process?\par
\f1\fs20\cf0\b\ltrpar\qr\sb60\sa0\li0\ri0\fi0 (1)\par
